---
import { LIGHT_SECONDS_PER_AU, blackouts, coverage, ephemeris, horizonsSnapshot } from '../sim/sources/horizons';
import { ALERT_BYTES, BUNDLE_OVERHEAD_BYTES, RAW_WINDOW_BYTES, RESIDUAL_BYTES } from '../sim/twin';
import { home } from '../site';
import SourceBadge from './SourceBadge.astro';
import TechTerm from './TechTerm.astro';

const minutes = ephemeris.distanceAu.map((au) => (au * LIGHT_SECONDS_PER_AU) / 60);
const range = coverage();
const longest = blackouts().reduce((best, window) => (window.days > best.days ? window : best));

const principles = [
  {
    name: 'Send the surprise, not the signal',
    text: 'The ground runs a copy of each astronaut’s reference model. The server sends only what that copy could not predict. With no link, the ground keeps projecting and shows how unsure it is.',
    term: 'predictive-coding',
  },
  {
    name: 'Store and forward, with custody',
    text: 'Data waits on board until the next hop can take it. Nothing depends on both ends being awake at once.',
    term: 'bundle-protocol',
  },
  {
    name: 'Priority by clinical value',
    text: `An alert summary of ${BUNDLE_OVERHEAD_BYTES + ALERT_BYTES} bytes leaves first. Routine updates follow. Raw windows travel only when the ground asks.`,
    term: null,
  },
  {
    name: 'Never wait for a resend',
    text: 'Asking again costs a round trip of up to 40 minutes. Each message leaves with repair packets, and the ground rebuilds it from whichever ones arrive.',
    term: 'erasure-coding',
  },
  {
    name: 'A record the ground can verify',
    text: 'Events go into an append-only log. The ground can prove nothing is missing, ask only for the gaps, and merge the same record twice without harm.',
    term: 'ledger',
  },
  {
    name: 'Scheduled around contact',
    text: 'The server knows when the link will be there and what fits in each pass. A solar conjunction is planned for, not discovered.',
    term: null,
  },
];
---
<!-- Store and forward was tested in the field: a slice of birthday cake, saved on a plate, delivered when the recipient woke from a nap. Nothing lost, nothing duplicated. -->
<section class="section" id="link">
  <p class="eyebrow">04 / Spectra Link</p>
  <h2 class="section-title">The crew is never waiting on Earth. Earth is never left guessing.</h2>
  <p class="section-lede">
    Between Mars and Earth a message takes {Math.min(...minutes).toFixed(0)} to {Math.max(...minutes).toFixed(0)} minutes
    each way, and for {longest.days} days around {longest.start.slice(0, 4)} the Sun blocks the path entirely.
    Spectra Link is our proposal for a link that works anyway.
  </p>
  <p class="link-basis">
    <SourceBadge kind="data" source="JPL Horizons" date={horizonsSnapshot.retrievedAt} />
    Light time and blackout from the Earth to Mars ephemeris, {range.start.slice(0, 4)} to {range.end.slice(0, 4)}.
  </p>

  <ol class="steps principles">
    {principles.map((principle) => (
      <li>
        <h3>{principle.name}</h3>
        <p>{principle.text}</p>
        {principle.term && <p class="principle-term"><TechTerm id={principle.term} /></p>}
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <p>
    A quiet ten-second window costs nothing to send. One that leaves the pattern costs {RESIDUAL_BYTES} bytes,
    against {RAW_WINDOW_BYTES} for the raw readings.
  </p>
  <p class="source">
    Spectra Link is a proposal. The simulator plays it out with a delay, outages, packet loss and a
    server restart; it does not implement the network standards it names.{' '}
    <a href={`${home}demo/`}>Disturb the link in the simulator</a>.
  </p>
</section>
